    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The pervasive belief in the revolution, that the common struggles of the *Ancien Régime* simply provided the necessary tinder, is a profound oversimplification of the true political fire. It was *Danton and the like who provided the fuel, but it was the absolute, unbending ideological discipline of the Incorruptible that provided the necessary, relentless oxygen for the whole inferno to claim the nation for its absolute will.\n\nWithout the specific, fervent, and unwavering moral absolutism that defined Robespierre, the revolutionary fervor, however strong in the common *sans-culotte*, would have predictably devolved into political factionalism, a predictable and ultimately *stagnant* argument for change. He was not just a strong leader in a strong time, but the very necessary, absolute force that forced the transition from a political debate to a divine and uncompromising act of political, moral, and national *re-forging",
      "source": "target",
